WHAT IS COVERED BY THAT LICENCE
-------------------------------
Everything in this repository: the measurement core (src/tripphysics/eval.py
and the rest of the package), the synthetic data generator, the attack
scripts, the tests, and the documentation. You may run it, read it, fork it
and reuse it under the MIT terms, including inside a commercial evaluation.

The point of the permissive licence is that the measurement is auditable and
reusable. A metric you are not allowed to inspect is not evidence.

WHAT IS NOT IN THIS REPOSITORY
------------------------------
Real data of any kind, and any detector tuned on real data. Everything here
runs on the synthetic population described below.

DATA PROVENANCE
---------------
All data shipped or generated here is synthetic. It is produced by the
generator in this repository from a fixed seed. No dataset from any company,
customer or third party is included, and none was used to build it. No
personal data of any kind is present.

The consequence is stated throughout the documentation and repeated here so it
cannot be missed: numbers produced on this synthetic population describe the
generator, not anyone's real traffic. The harness exists so the same
measurement can be re-run inside your perimeter on your own logs, where the
result would describe your traffic instead.

